[
  {
    "id": "g-past-ar",
    "title": "-ar verbs in the past",
    "summary": "what happened: falei, comprei, cheguei",
    "intro": [
      "This past tense (the *pretérito* perfeito) is for finished actions: *Ontem falei com a Ana* = Yesterday I spoke to Ana.",
      "For -ar verbs, take off -ar and add: -ei, -aste, -ou, -ámos, -aram. Here is *falar*:"
    ],
    "tables": [
      { "verb": "falar", "meaning": "to speak", "caption": "Past tense of falar", "rows": [
        { "person": "eu", "form": "falei" },
        { "person": "tu", "form": "falaste" },
        { "person": "ele / ela / você", "form": "falou" },
        { "person": "nós", "form": "falámos" },
        { "person": "eles / elas / vocês", "form": "falaram" }
      ] }
    ],
    "examples": [
      { "pt": "Ontem trabalhei até tarde.", "en": "I worked late yesterday." },
      { "pt": "Compraste o pão?", "en": "Did you buy the bread?" },
      { "pt": "O comboio chegou às dez.", "en": "The train arrived at ten." },
      { "pt": "Jantámos fora no sábado.", "en": "We ate out on Saturday." }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "In Portugal, *falámos* (we spoke) has an accent to tell it apart from *falamos* (we speak). Typed without it, it counts here, but you'll be shown the right spelling.",
      "The *eu* form changes its spelling to keep the sound: *chegar* → *cheguei*, *ficar* → *fiquei*, *começar* → *comecei*.",
      "There's no \"did\" in Portuguese questions, just the past form: *Compraste o pão*? = Did you buy the bread?",
      "Time words that go with it: *ontem* (yesterday), no *sábado passado* (last Saturday), *na semana passada* (last week), *há dois dias* (two days ago)."
    ],
    "drills": [
      { "type": "form", "verb": "falar", "person": "eu", "answer": "falei" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "comprar", "person": "tu", "answer": "compraste" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "trabalhar", "person": "ela", "answer": "trabalhou" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "jantar", "person": "nós", "answer": "jantámos" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "chegar", "person": "eu", "answer": "cheguei" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "ficar", "person": "eu", "answer": "fiquei" },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "trabalhar", "before": "Ontem eu ", "after": " até tarde.", "answer": "trabalhei", "en": "I worked late yesterday." },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "comprar", "before": "Tu ", "after": " o pão?", "answer": "compraste", "en": "Did you buy the bread?" },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "chegar", "before": "O comboio ", "after": " às dez.", "answer": "chegou", "en": "The train arrived at ten." },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "jantar", "before": "Nós ", "after": " fora no sábado.", "answer": "jantámos", "en": "We ate out on Saturday." },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "ficar", "before": "Eles ", "after": " o dia todo na praia.", "answer": "ficaram", "en": "They spent the whole day at the beach." },
      { "type": "rewrite", "verb": "falar", "from": "Hoje falo com a Ana.", "before": "Ontem ", "after": " com a Ana.", "answer": "falei", "en": "Yesterday I spoke to Ana." },
      { "type": "rewrite", "verb": "trabalhar", "from": "Hoje a Rita trabalha em casa.", "before": "Ontem a Rita ", "after": " em casa.", "answer": "trabalhou", "en": "Yesterday Rita worked from home." },
      { "type": "rewrite", "verb": "começar", "from": "Hoje começo cedo.", "before": "Ontem ", "after": " cedo.", "answer": "comecei", "en": "Yesterday I started early." }
    ],
    "verified": false
  },
  {
    "id": "g-past-er-ir",
    "title": "-er and -ir verbs in the past",
    "summary": "comi, bebi, percebi, abri",
    "intro": [
      "For -er verbs, take off -er and add: -i, -este, -eu, -emos, -eram.",
      "For -ir verbs, take off -ir and add: -i, -iste, -iu, -imos, -iram.",
      "The *nós* form is the same as in the present (*comemos*, *partimos*). The sentence tells you which one is meant."
    ],
    "tables": [
      { "verb": "comer", "meaning": "to eat", "caption": "Past tense of comer", "rows": [
        { "person": "eu", "form": "comi" },
        { "person": "tu", "form": "comeste" },
        { "person": "ele / ela / você", "form": "comeu" },
        { "person": "nós", "form": "comemos" },
        { "person": "eles / elas / vocês", "form": "comeram" }
      ] },
      { "verb": "partir", "meaning": "to leave", "caption": "Past tense of partir", "rows": [
        { "person": "eu", "form": "parti" },
        { "person": "tu", "form": "partiste" },
        { "person": "ele / ela / você", "form": "partiu" },
        { "person": "nós", "form": "partimos" },
        { "person": "eles / elas / vocês", "form": "partiram" }
      ] }
    ],
    "examples": [
      { "pt": "Comi bacalhau ao almoço.", "en": "I had salt cod for lunch." },
      { "pt": "Bebeste o meu café?", "en": "Did you drink my coffee?" },
      { "pt": "Desculpe, não percebi.", "en": "Sorry, I didn't understand." },
      { "pt": "A loja abriu às nove.", "en": "The shop opened at nine." }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "*Não percebi* (I didn't understand) is one of the most useful phrases you can learn.",
      "Some verbs that are irregular in the present are regular here: dormi, pedi, ouvi, *saí*.",
      "Others are irregular in the past too (*fazer*, *dizer*, *ver*, *vir*…). They're in the next topics."
    ],
    "drills": [
      { "type": "form", "verb": "comer", "person": "eu", "answer": "comi" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "beber", "person": "tu", "answer": "bebeste" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "perceber", "person": "ela", "answer": "percebeu" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "viver", "person": "nós", "answer": "vivemos" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "abrir", "person": "eles", "answer": "abriram" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "decidir", "person": "eu", "answer": "decidi" },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "comer", "before": "Eu ", "after": " bacalhau ao almoço.", "answer": "comi", "en": "I had salt cod for lunch." },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "perceber", "before": "Desculpa, não ", "after": ".", "answer": "percebi", "en": "Sorry, I didn't understand." },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "abrir", "before": "A loja ", "after": " às nove.", "answer": "abriu", "en": "The shop opened at nine." },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "partir", "before": "Eles ", "after": " ontem para Lisboa.", "answer": "partiram", "en": "They left for Lisbon yesterday." },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "dormir", "before": "Tu ", "after": " bem esta noite?", "answer": "dormiste", "en": "Did you sleep well last night?" },
      { "type": "rewrite", "verb": "beber", "from": "Hoje bebo água.", "before": "Ontem ", "after": " água.", "answer": "bebi", "en": "Yesterday I drank water." },
      { "type": "rewrite", "verb": "escrever", "from": "Hoje a Ana escreve ao pai.", "before": "Ontem a Ana ", "after": " ao pai.", "answer": "escreveu", "en": "Yesterday Ana wrote to her father." },
      { "type": "rewrite", "verb": "abrir", "from": "Hoje eles abrem a janela.", "before": "Ontem eles ", "after": " a janela.", "answer": "abriram", "en": "Yesterday they opened the window." }
    ],
    "verified": false
  },
  {
    "id": "g-past-fui-tive-estive",
    "title": "fui, tive, estive",
    "summary": "ser, ir, ter and estar in the past",
    "intro": [
      "The most common verbs are irregular in the past, so learn them as tables.",
      "Ser and *ir* share the same past forms: *fui* means \"I was\" or \"I went\". The sentence tells you which: *Fui ao Porto* (I went to Porto), *Foi ótimo* (it was great)."
    ],
    "tables": [
      { "verb": "ser / ir", "meaning": "to be / to go", "caption": "Past tense of ser and ir", "rows": [
        { "person": "eu", "form": "fui" },
        { "person": "tu", "form": "foste" },
        { "person": "ele / ela / você", "form": "foi" },
        { "person": "nós", "form": "fomos" },
        { "person": "eles / elas / vocês", "form": "foram" }
      ] },
      { "verb": "ter", "meaning": "to have", "caption": "Past tense of ter", "rows": [
        { "person": "eu", "form": "tive" },
        { "person": "tu", "form": "tiveste" },
        { "person": "ele / ela / você", "form": "teve" },
        { "person": "nós", "form": "tivemos" },
        { "person": "eles / elas / vocês", "form": "tiveram" }
      ] },
      { "verb": "estar", "meaning": "to be (how, where)", "caption": "Past tense of estar", "rows": [
        { "person": "eu", "form": "estive" },
        { "person": "tu", "form": "estiveste" },
        { "person": "ele / ela / você", "form": "esteve" },
        { "person": "nós", "form": "estivemos" },
        { "person": "eles / elas / vocês", "form": "estiveram" }
      ] }
    ],
    "examples": [
      { "pt": "Fui ao Porto no fim de semana.", "en": "I went to Porto at the weekend." },
      { "pt": "Foi muito bom.", "en": "It was really good." },
      { "pt": "Tive um dia difícil.", "en": "I had a hard day." },
      { "pt": "Onde estiveste ontem?", "en": "Where were you yesterday?" }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Ser and estar split the same way as in the present: *Foi simpático* (he was nice), *Esteve doente* (he was ill).",
      "*Como foi*? = How was it?"
    ],
    "drills": [
      { "type": "form", "verb": "ir", "person": "eu", "answer": "fui" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "ser", "person": "ela", "answer": "foi" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "ir", "person": "nós", "answer": "fomos" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "ter", "person": "eu", "answer": "tive" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "ter", "person": "ele", "answer": "teve" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "estar", "person": "tu", "answer": "estiveste" },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "ir", "before": "Eu ", "after": " ao Porto no fim de semana.", "answer": "fui", "en": "I went to Porto at the weekend." },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "ser", "before": "O jantar ", "after": " muito bom.", "answer": "foi", "en": "Dinner was really good." },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "ter", "before": "Ontem ", "after": " um dia difícil.", "answer": "tive", "en": "Yesterday I had a hard day." },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "estar", "before": "Onde ", "after": " tu ontem?", "answer": "estiveste", "en": "Where were you yesterday?" },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "ir", "before": "Eles ", "after": " à praia.", "answer": "foram", "en": "They went to the beach." },
      { "type": "rewrite", "verb": "estar", "from": "Hoje estou em casa.", "before": "Ontem ", "after": " em casa.", "answer": "estive", "en": "Yesterday I was at home." },
      { "type": "rewrite", "verb": "ir", "from": "Hoje vou ao cinema.", "before": "Ontem ", "after": " ao cinema.", "answer": "fui", "en": "Yesterday I went to the cinema." },
      { "type": "rewrite", "verb": "ter", "from": "Hoje temos aulas.", "before": "Ontem ", "after": " aulas.", "answer": "tivemos", "en": "Yesterday we had classes." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "O Pedro ", "after": " doente na semana passada.", "options": ["esteve", "foi"], "answer": "esteve", "en": "Pedro was ill last week.", "why": "Being ill is a state that changes: estar, so *esteve*." }
    ],
    "verified": false
  },
  {
